      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <div id="tx6-vs-glowup" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">2. TX6, TX6-GlowUp, “GlowUp Edition”: Is There a Difference?</h2>
<p>
            People search for this machine under several names — the LifeSpan TX6, the TX6-GlowUp,
            the “TX6 GlowUp edition” — as if they might be different products. As far as we can
            establish, they are not. LifeSpan’s own US store sells one model, the TX6-GlowUp Under
            Desk Treadmill, in two colours, Timeless Black and Pristine White. The Amazon listing for
            the same machine calls it the “LifeSpan Fitness TX6 Under Desk Treadmill”, and the
            independent tracker we read records TX6 as the part number and model name and TX6-GlowUp
            as the marketing name. It lists the machine as first available on Amazon in January 2024.
          </p>
          <p>
            “GlowUp” is LifeSpan’s name for its current generation of desk treadmills, not a TX6
            option. The TR1200Pro and the TR5000B Pro+ carry it too. It distinguishes the current
            machines from LifeSpan’s older TR1200-DT3 and TR5000-DT5 desk treadmills, which used the
            same model numbers with different consoles and figures. That matters if you are reading
            reviews or buying used: a review of a TR1200-DT3 says nothing reliable about a TX6, and
            neither does an Amazon star rating gathered across several LifeSpan models.
          </p>
          <p>
            That last point is worth taking seriously. The tracker reports that the Amazon listing
            the TX6 sits on shares its customer reviews with the TR1200 and TR5000 and includes reviews
            from 2017, years before the TX6 existed. An average score on that listing is therefore a
            score for LifeSpan desk treadmills in general, not for this one. We do not print ratings
            on this site, and this is a good example of why.
          </p>
        </div>

