        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">The LifeSpan TX6-GlowUp is worth its price for one kind of buyer</strong>:
            someone heavier or taller than a budget pad is built for, who will walk at a desk for
            several hours most days. Its 20-inch belt, 400 lb rating, seven-hour daily figure and
            ten-year frame warranty hold up across sources; its weight, step-up height and motor
            figures do not, and LifeSpan publishes no continuous motor rating.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy it at LifeSpan’s sale price of about $1,300 to $1,400, plan the desk from a 5.8-inch
            step-up and a non-GFCI outlet, and read the return terms first. If you walk an hour a day,
            the <a href="/best-walking-pads/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">best walking pads</a>
